{"name":"Night Market","hex":"#4c6177","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night market","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A market that only operates at night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night_market"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night market","blocks":[{"text":"Night markets or night bazaars are street markets which operate at night and are generally dedicated to more leisurely strolling, shopping, and eating than more businesslike day markets. The culture of night markets originates from China and have spread globally with overseas Chinese populations. They are typically open-air markets popular in East Asia, Southeast Asia, and Chinatowns in several other regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Myeongdong_night_market_seoul_4.jpg/330px-Myeongdong_night_market_seoul_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_market","wikidata":"Q1962840"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg/500px-TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg/1280px-TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg/500px-TWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Taipei's Shilin Night Market indoor area.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATWShiLinNightMarketRichy2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg/500px-Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg/1280px-Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg/500px-Night_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Night market in Chiang Mai, Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANight_Market_Chiang_Mai.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu